          %h3#InTermsOfRepresentableFunctors In terms of representable functors
          %p
            The condition
            %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:HomIsomorphismForAdjointFunctors"} (1)
            on adjoint functors
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                  %mo ⊣
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L \dashv R
            in Def.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#AdjointFunctorsInTermsOfNaturalBijectionOfHomSets"}
            implies in particular that for every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"} object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi d
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi 𝒟
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d \in \mathcal{D}
            the functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Hom
                    %mi 𝒟
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi L
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mi d
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Hom_{\mathcal{D}}(L(-),d)
            is a
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representable+functor"} representable functor
            with
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representing+object"} representing object
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R(d)
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#AdjointFunctorFromObjectwiseRepresentingObject"}
            observes that the existence of such
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representing+objects"} representing objects
            for all
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi d
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d
            is, in fact, already sufficient to imply that there is a right adjoint functor.
          %p This equivalent perspective on adjoint functors makes manifest that:
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                adjoint functors are, if they exist, unique up to natural isomorphism, this is Prop.
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#UniquenessOfAdjoints"}
                below;
            %li
              %p
                the concept of adjoint functors makes sense also
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relative+adjoint+functor"} relative
                to a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
                on which representing objects exists, this is the content of Remark
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#RelativeAdjointFunctors"}
                below.
          %h4#global_definition Global definition
          #AdjointFunctorFromObjectwiseRepresentingObject.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_3 Proposition
            %p
              %strong
                (adjoint functor from objectwise
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representing+object"} representing object
            %p
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi 𝒟
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L \;\colon\; \mathcal{C} \longrightarrow \mathcal{D}
              has a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+adjoint"} right adjoint
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
