            %h6#proof_3 Proof
            %p Notice that
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  in the language of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaves"} presheaves
                  the assumption is that for each
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi d
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi 𝒟
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d \in \mathcal{D}
                  the presheaf
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Hom
                          %mi 𝒟
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi L
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ,
                        %mi d
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo ∈
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %msup
                          %mi 𝒞
                          %mi op
                        %mo ,
                        %mi Set
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        Hom_{\mathcal{D}}(L(-),d)
                        \\;\in\;
                        [\mathcal{C}^{op}, Set]
                %p
                  is
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representable+functor"} represented
                  by the object
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi R
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi d
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R(d)
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformation"} naturally
                  so.
              %li
                %p
                  In terms of the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+embedding"} Yoneda embedding
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi y
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mi 𝒞
                        %mo ↪
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %msup
                          %mi 𝒞
                          %mi op
                        %mo ,
                        %mi Set
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        y
                        \\;\colon\;
                        \\mathcal{C}
                        \\hookrightarrow
                        [\mathcal{C}^{op}, Set]
                %p we have
                #eq:YonedanotationForRepresentable.maruku-equation
                  %span.maruku-eq-number (6)
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Hom
                          %mi 𝒞
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo ,
                        %mi R
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi d
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %mi y
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi R
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi d
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        Hom_{\mathcal{C}}(-,R(d))
                        \=
                        y(R(d))
            %p
              The condition
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:NaturalitySquareForAdjointnessOfFunctors"} (2)
              says equivalently that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              has to be such that for all
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi h
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi d
                      %mn 1
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi d
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h \;\colon\; d_1 \to d_2
              the following diagram in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+presheaves"} category of presheaves
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\mathcal{C}^{op}, Set]
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commuting+diagram"} commutes
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi Hom
                              %mi 𝒟
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi L
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ,
                            %msub
                              %mi d
                              %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %munderover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mo ≃
                              %mover
                                %mrow
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mo ˜
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi Hom
                              %mi 𝒞
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mo ,
                            %mi R
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi d
                              %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi Hom
                                    %mi 𝒞
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %mi L
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                  %mo ,
                                  %mi h
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi Hom
                                    %mi 𝒞
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                  %mo ,
                                  %mi R
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %mi h
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi Hom
                              %mi 𝒟
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi L
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ,
                            %msub
                              %mi d
                              %mn 2
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %munderover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mo ≃
                              %mover
                                %mrow
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mo ˜
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi Hom
                              %mi 𝒞
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mo ,
                            %mi R
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi d
                              %mn 2
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    Hom_{\mathcal{D}}(L(-),d_1)
                    \&amp;\underoverset{\simeq}{\widetilde{(-)}}{\longrightarrow}&amp;
                    Hom_{\mathcal{C}}(-,R(d_1))
                    \\\
                    {}^{\mathllap{ Hom_{\mathcal{C}}( L(-) , h ) }}
                    \\big\downarrow
                    \&amp;&amp;
                    \\big\downarrow^{\mathrlap{ Hom_{\mathcal{C}}( -, R(h)  ) }}
                    \\\
                    Hom_{\mathcal{D}}(L(-),d_2)
                    \&amp;\underoverset{\simeq}{\widetilde{(-)}}{\longrightarrow}&amp;
                    Hom_{\mathcal{C}}(-, R(d_2))
                    }
            %p This manifestly has a unique solution
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi h
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mi 𝒞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi h
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    y(R(h))
                    \\;=\;
                    Hom_{\mathcal{C}}(-,R(h))
            %p
              for every morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi h
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msub
                      %mi d
                      %mn 1
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi d
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h \colon d_1 \to d_2
              under
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y(R(-))
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:YonedanotationForRepresentable"} (6)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+embedding"} Yoneda embedding
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fully+faithful+functor"} fully faithful functor
              (
              %a{:href => "Yoneda+embedding#YonedaEmbeddingIsFullyFaithful"}> this prop.
              ), which means that thereby also
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi h
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R(h)
              is uniquely fixed.
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              In more fancy language, the statement of Prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#AdjointFunctorFromObjectwiseRepresentingObject"}
              is the following:
            %p
              By precomposition
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
              defines a functor of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf+categories"} presheaf categories
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi L
                      %mo *
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝒟
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    L^* \;\colon\; [\mathcal{D}^{op}, Set] \to [\mathcal{C}^{op}, Set]
                    \\,.
            %p
              By
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/restriction"} restriction
              along the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+embedding"} Yoneda embedding
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi 𝒟
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝒟
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y \;\colon\; \mathcal{D} \to [\mathcal{D}^{op}, Set]
              this yields the functor
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi L
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi 𝒟
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mi y
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %msup
                              %mi 𝒟
                              %mi op
                            %mo ,
                            %mi Set
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %msup
                                  %mi L
                                  %mo *
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %msup
                              %mi 𝒞
                              %mi op
                            %mo ,
                            %mi Set
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi d
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↦
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi Hom
                              %mi 𝒟
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mo ,
                            %mi d
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↦
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi Hom
                              %mi 𝒟
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi L
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ,
                            %mi d
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\bar L
                    \\;\colon\;
                    \\array{
                    \\mathcal{D}
                    \&amp;\overset{y}{\longrightarrow}&amp;
                    [\mathcal{D}^{op}, Set]
                    \&amp;\overset{L^*}{\longrightarrow}&amp;
                    [\mathcal{C}^{op}, Set]
                    \\\
                    d
                    \&amp;\mapsto&amp;
                    Hom_{\mathcal{D}}(-,d)
                    \&amp;\mapsto&amp;
                    Hom_{\mathcal{D}}(L(-),d)
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              The statement is that for all
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d \in D
              this presheaf
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi L
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bar L(d)
              is
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representable+functor"} representable
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi 𝒟
                    %mo →
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R \colon \mathcal{D} \to \mathcal{C}
              such that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi L
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≃
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi y
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi R
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\bar L \;\simeq\; y \circ R
                    \\,.
          %h4#LocalDefinition Local definition
          #RelativeAdjointFunctors.num_remark
            %h6#remark_2 Remark
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relative+adjoint+functors"}> relative adjoint functors
                )
            %p
              The perspective of Prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#AdjointFunctorFromObjectwiseRepresentingObject"}
              has the advantage that it yields useful information even if the adjoint functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              does not exist globally, i.e. as a functor on all of
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒟
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{D}
            %p It may happen that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi L
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≔
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mi D
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi L
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∈
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\bar L(d) \coloneqq Hom_D(L(-),d) \in [C^{op}, Set]
            %p
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representable+functor"} representable
              for
              %em some
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"} object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi 𝒟
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d \in \mathcal{D}
              but not for all
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi d
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R(d)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
              %em relative to
              the inclusion of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
              determined by those
              = succeed "s" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi L
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bar L(d)
              is representable; see
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflection+along+a+functor"} reflection along a functor
              and
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relative+adjoint+functor"} relative adjoint functor
              for more.
            %p
              This
              %em global
              versus
              %em local
              evaluation of adjoint functors induces the global/local pictures of the definitions
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limit"} limit
                  \/
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+limit"} homotopy limit
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+extension"} Kan extension
            %p as discussed there.
          %h3#UniversalArrows In terms of universal factorization through a (co)unit
          %p
            We have seen in Prop.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#GeneralAdjunctsInTermsOfAdjunctionUnitCounit"}
            that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unit+of+an+adjunction"} unit of an adjunction
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/counit+of+an+adjunction"} counit of an adjunction
            plays a special role. One may amplify this by characterizing these morphisms as
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+arrows"} universal arrows
            in the sense of the following Def.
            = succeed "." do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#UniversalArrow"}
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CollectionOfUniversalArrowsEquivalentToAdjointFunctor"}
            below.
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
          #UniversalArrow.num_defn
            %h6#definition_4 Definition
            %p
              %strong (universal arrow)
            %p
              Given a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi 𝒟
                      %mo →
                      %mi 𝒞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R \;\colon\; \mathcal{D} \to \mathcal{C}
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi c
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi 𝒞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c\in \mathcal{C}
              %em universal arrow
              from
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi c
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c
              to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              (or a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflection+along+a+functor"} reflection
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi c
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c
              along
              = succeed ")" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/initial+object"} initial object
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/comma+category"} comma category
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi c
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi R
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (c/R)
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  an
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"} object
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi L
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi c
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi 𝒟
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L(c)\in \mathcal{D}
              %li
                %p
                  a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphism
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi η
                            %mi c
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mi c
                          %mo →
                          %mi R
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                          %mi L
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi c
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta_c \;\colon\; c \to R\big(L(c)\big)
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunction+unit"} unit
            %p
              such that for any
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi 𝒟
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d\in \mathcal{D}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi c
                    %mo →
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon c\to R(d)
              factors through this unit
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi η
                      %mi c
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta_c
              as
            #eq:UniversalArrowFactorization.maruku-equation
              %span.maruku-eq-number (7)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi c
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi η
                                    %mi c
                            %mo ↙
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo ↘
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi f
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi R
                            %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                            %mi L
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi c
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %mi R
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mover
                                  %mi f
                                  %mo ˜
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi R
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi d
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi L
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi c
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mover
                                %mi f
                                %mo ˜
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi d
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \&amp;&amp; c
                    \\\
                    \&amp;
                    {}^{\mathllap{\eta_c}}\swarrow
                    \&amp;&amp;
                    \\searrow^{\mathrlap{f}}
                    \\\
                    R\big(L(c)\big)
                    \&amp;&amp;
                    \\underset
                    {R (\widetilde f)}
                    {\longrightarrow}
                    \&amp;&amp;
                    R(d)
                    \\\
                    \\\
                    L(c)
                    \&amp;&amp;
                    \\underset{ \widetilde f}{\longrightarrow}
                    \&amp;&amp;
                    d
                    }
            %p
              for a unique
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mover
                        %mi f
                        %mo ˜
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi L
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi c
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mi d
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widetilde f  \;\colon\; L(c) \longrightarrow d
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunct"} adjunct
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
          %p
            (e.g.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Borceux94"} Borceux, Vol. 1, Definition 3.1.1
          #UniversalMorphismsAreInitialObjectsInCommaCategory.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_4 Proposition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+morphisms"} universal morphisms
                are
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/initial+objects"} initial objects
                in the
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/comma+category"} comma category
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                    %mo :
                    %mi 𝒟
                    %mo →
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R: \mathcal{D} \to \mathcal{C}
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi c
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c \in \mathcal{C}
              an
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"} object
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi c
                        %mover
                          %mo →
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi η
                              %mi c
                        %mi R
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi L
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi c
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c \overset{\eta_c}{\to} R(L(c))
                  is a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+morphism"} universal morphism
                  into
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi R
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi L
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi c
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R(L(c))
                  (Def.
                  = succeed ");" do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#UniversalArrow"}
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi c
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi η
                          %mi c
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (c, \eta_c)
                  is the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/initial+object"} initial object
                  in the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/comma+category"} comma category
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi c
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mi R
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c/R
          #CollectionOfUniversalArrowsEquivalentToAdjointFunctor.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_5 Proposition
            %p
              %strong
                (collection of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+arrows"} universal arrows
                equivalent to
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+functor"} adjoint functor
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi 𝒟
                    %mo →
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R \;\colon\; \mathcal{D} \to \mathcal{C}
              be a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi R
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
                  has a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
                  functor
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi L
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mi 𝒞
                        %mo →
                        %mi 𝒟
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L \colon \mathcal{C} \to \mathcal{D}
                  according to Def.
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#AdjointFunctorsInTermsOfNaturalBijectionOfHomSets"}
              %li
                %p
                  for every
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"} object
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi c
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi 𝒞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c \in \mathcal{C}
                  there is a universal arrow
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi c
                          %mover
                            %mo ⟶
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi η
                                %mi c
                          %mi R
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi L
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi c
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c \overset{\eta_c}{\longrightarrow} R(L(c))
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#UniversalArrow"}
          .proof
            %h6#proof_4 Proof
            %p
              In one direction, assume a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
              is given. Define the would-be universal arrow at
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi c
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c \in \mathcal{C}
              to be the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unit+of+an+adjunction"} unit of the adjunction
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi η
                      %mi c
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta_c
              via Def.
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#AdjunctionUnitFromHomIsomorphism"}
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#GeneralAdjunctsInTermsOfAdjunctionUnitCounit"}
            %p
              In the other direction, assume that universal arrows
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi η
                      %mi c
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta_c
              are given. The uniqueness clause in Def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#UniversalArrow"}
              immediately implies
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bijections"} bijections
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi Hom
                              %mi 𝒟
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi L
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi c
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ,
                            %mi d
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mo ≃
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi Hom
                              %mi 𝒞
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi c
                            %mo ,
                            %mi R
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi d
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mrow
                              %mo (
                              %mi L
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi c
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mover
                                %mo →
                                %mover
                                  %mi f
                                  %mo ˜
                              %mi d
                              %mo )
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↦
                          %mtd
                            %mrow
                              %mo (
                              %mi c
                              %mover
                                %mo →
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi η
                                    %mi c
                              %mi R
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi L
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi c
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mover
                                %mo →
                                %mrow
                                  %mi R
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %mover
                                    %mi f
                                    %mo ˜
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mi R
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi d
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    Hom_{\mathcal{D}}(L(c),d)
                    \&amp;\overset{\simeq}{\longrightarrow}&amp;
                    Hom_{\mathcal{C}}(c,R(d))
                    \\\
                    \\left(
                    L(c) \overset{\widetilde f}{\to} d
                    \\right)
                    \&amp;\mapsto&amp;
                    \\left(
                    c \overset{\eta_c}{\to} R(L(c)) \overset{ R(\widetilde f) }{\to} R(d)
                    \\right)
                    }
            %p
              Hence to satisfy
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:HomIsomorphismForAdjointFunctors"} (1)
              it remains to show that these are
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformation"} natural
              in both variables. In fact, by Prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#AdjointFunctorFromObjectwiseRepresentingObject"}
              it is sufficient to show naturality in the variable
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              applied in
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:UniversalArrowFactorization"} (7)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi h
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msub
                      %mi d
                      %mn 1
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi d
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h \colon d_1 \to d_2
              any
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi c
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi η
                                    %mi c
                            %mo ↙
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo ↘
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi f
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi R
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi L
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi c
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %mi R
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mover
                                  %mi f
                                  %mo ˜
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi R
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi d
                              %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mi R
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %mi h
                                  %mo ∘
                                  %mover
                                    %mi f
                                    %mo ˜
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ↘
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mi R
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %mi h
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi R
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi d
                              %mn 2
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \&amp;&amp; c
                    \\\
                    \&amp; {}^{\mathllap{\eta_c}}\swarrow &amp;&amp; \searrow^{\mathrlap{f}}
                    \\\
                    R (L(c)) &amp;&amp;\underset{R (\widetilde f)}{\longrightarrow}&amp;&amp; R(d_1)
                    \\\
                    \&amp;&amp; {}_{\mathllap{ R( h\circ \widetilde f ) }}\searrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{R(h)}}
                    \\\
                    \&amp;&amp; &amp;&amp; R(d_2)
                    }
          .num_example
            %h6#example Example
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localization"} localization
                via
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+arrows"} universal arrows
            %p
              The characterization of adjoint functors in terms of universal factorizations through the unit and counit (Prop.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CollectionOfUniversalArrowsEquivalentToAdjointFunctor"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+and+faithful+functor"} full and faithful functor
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi 𝒟
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    R \;\colon\;
                    \\mathcal{D} \hookrightarrow \mathcal{C}
            %p
              exhibiting
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒟
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{D}
              as a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflective+subcategory"} reflective subcategory
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
              as a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localization"} localization
              and of objects in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/essential+image"} essential image
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
              as
              = succeed "." do
                %strong local objects
            %ul
              %li
                every morphism
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi c
                      %mo →
                      %mi R
                      %mi d
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c \to R d
                from
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi c
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c
                into a local object factors throught the localization of
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi c
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c
          %h3#InTermsOfCommaCategories In terms of comma categories
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi C
                  %mo →
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L \colon C \to D
            is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
            to a functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi D
                  %mo →
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R \colon D \to C
            if and only if there is an isomorphism (not
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence"} equivalence
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/comma+categories"} comma categories
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                  %mi D
                  %mo ≅
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L \downarrow D \cong C \downarrow R
            and this isomorphism commutes with the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/forgetful+functors"} forgetful functors
            to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product+category"} product category
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo ×
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C \times D
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Functorial+Semantics+of+Algebraic+Theories"} Functorial Semantics of Algebraic Theories
          %p
            This characterisation generalises (in the unenriched setting) to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relative+adjunctions"} relative adjunctions
            by replacing
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C \downarrow R
            by
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi J
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J \downarrow R
          %h3#InTermsOfCographsHeteromorphisms In terms of cographs/correspondences/heteromorphisms
          %p
            Every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/profunctor"} profunctor
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                  %mo :
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mi op
                  %mo ×
                  %mi D
                  %mo →
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  k : C^{op} \times D \to S
          %p
            defines a category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %msup
                    %mo *
                    %mi k
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C *^k D
            with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Obj
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %msup
                    %mo *
                    %mi k
                  %mi D
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi Obj
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⊔
                  %mi Obj
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi D
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Obj(C *^k D) = Obj(C) \sqcup Obj(D)
            and with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom+set"} hom set
            given by
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Hom
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                      %msup
                        %mo *
                        %mi k
                      %mi D
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mrow
                    %mo {
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi Hom
                              %mi C
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo ,
                            %mi Y
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mi if
                            %mi X
                            %mo ,
                            %mi Y
                            %mo ∈
                            %mi C
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi Hom
                              %mi D
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo ,
                            %mi Y
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mi if
                            %mi X
                            %mo ,
                            %mi Y
                            %mo ∈
                            %mi D
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi k
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo ,
                            %mi Y
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mi if
                            %mi X
                            %mo ∈
                            %mi C
                            %mi and
                            %mi Y
                            %mo ∈
                            %mi D
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi ∅
                          %mtd
                            %mi otherwise
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Hom_{C *^k D}(X,Y)
                  \=
                  \\left\{
                  \\array{
                  Hom_C(X,Y) &amp; if X, Y \in C
                  \\\
                  Hom_D(X,Y) &amp; if X,Y \in D
                  \\\
                  k(X,Y) &amp; if X \in C and Y \in D
                  \\\
                  \\emptyset &amp; otherwise
                  }
                  \\right.
          %p
            (An element of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k(X,Y)
            is also called a
            = succeed ")." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/heteromorphism"} heteromorphism
          %p
            This category naturally comes with a functor to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/interval"} interval
            category
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %msup
                    %mo *
                    %mi k
                  %mi D
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi Δ
                    %mn 1
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  C *^k D \to \Delta^1
                  \\,.
          %p
            Now, every functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                  %mo :
                  %mi C
                  %mo →
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L : C \to D
            induces a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/profunctor"} profunctor
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi k
                    %mi L
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi Hom
                    %mi D
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi L
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  k^L(X,Y) = Hom_D(L(X), Y)
          %p
            and every functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                  %mo :
                  %mi D
                  %mo →
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R : D \to C
            induces a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/profunctor"} profunctor
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi k
                    %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi Hom
                    %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  k_R(X,Y) = Hom_C(X, R(Y))
                  \\,.
          %p
            The functors
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            are adjoint precisely if the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/profunctors"} profunctors
            that they define in the above way are equivalent. This in turn is the case if
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %msup
                      %mo ⋆
                      %mi L
                    %mi D
                    %mo ≃
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi D
                      %mi op
                    %msup
                      %mo ⋆
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi R
                          %mi op
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mi op
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C \star^L D \simeq (D^{op} \star^{R^{op}} C^{op})^{op}
          %p
            We say that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %msup
                    %mo ⋆
                    %mi k
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C \star^k D
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cograph+of+a+functor"} cograph of the functor
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
          %h3#in_terms_of_graphs2sided_discrete_fibrations In terms of graphs/2-sided discrete fibrations
          %p
            Functors
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi C
                  %mo →
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L \colon C \to D
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi D
                  %mo →
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R \colon D \to C
            are adjoint precisely if we have a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+diagram"} commutative diagram
            of the form
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi L
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %msub
                            %mi Id
                            %mi D
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mo ≅
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi Id
                            %mi C
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mi R
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↘
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↙
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi C
                          %mo ×
                          %mi D
                          %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                            %mrow
                              %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                              %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  (L \downarrow Id_D)
                  \&amp;&amp;\stackrel{\cong}{\to}&amp;&amp;
                  (Id_C \downarrow R)
                  \\\
                  \&amp; \searrow &amp;&amp; \swarrow
                  \\\
                  \&amp;&amp;
                  C \times D
                  \\mathrlap{\,,}
                  }
          %p
            where the downwards arrows denote the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/maps"} maps
            induced by the canonical projections out of the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/comma+categories"} comma categories
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lawvere"} Lawvere
            in
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Functorial+Semantics+of+Algebraic+Theories"} Functorial Semantics of Algebraic Theories
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/comma+categories"} comma categories
          %p
            The above
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagram"} diagram
            may be recovered directly from the image under the equivalence
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mi op
                  %mo ×
                  %mi D
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Set
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mo ≃
                  %mi DFib
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi D
                  %mo ,
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [C^{op} \times D, Set] \stackrel{\simeq}{\to} DFib(D,C)
            described at
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-sided+fibration"} 2-sided fibration
            of the isomorphism of induced
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/profunctors"} profunctors
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mi op
                  %mo ×
                  %mi D
                  %mo →
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^{op} \times D \to Set
            (see above at “In terms of Hom isomorphism”). Its relation to the hom-set definition of adjoint functors can thus be understood within the general paradigm of
            = succeed "-like" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+construction"} Grothendieck construction
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category"} enriched adjunctions
          %p
            This description generalises to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relative+adjunctions"} relative adjunctions
            by replacing
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Id
                    %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Id_C
            with
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi J
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
          %h3#in_terms_of_kan_extensionsliftings In terms of Kan extensions/liftings
          %p
            Given
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi C
                    %mo →
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L \colon C \to D
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+adjoint"} right adjoint
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi D
                  %mo →
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R\colon D \to C
            precisely if the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+Kan+extension"} left Kan extension
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Lan
                    %mi L
                  %msub
                    %mn 1
                    %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Lan_L 1_C
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity"} identity
            along
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            exists and is
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+extension#AbsoluteKanExtension"} absolute
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                  %mo ≃
                  %msub
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Lan
                    %mi L
                  %msub
                    %mn 1
                    %mi C
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  R \simeq \mathop{Lan}_L 1_C
                  \\,.
          %p
            In this case, the universal 2-cell
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mn 1
                    %mi C
                  %mo →
                  %mi R
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1_C \to R L
            corresponds to the
            = succeed ";" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unit+of+an+adjunction"} unit of the adjunction
          %p
            It is also possible to express this in terms of Kan liftings:
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            has a right adjoint
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            if and only if:
          %ul
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Rift
                      %mi L
                    %msub
                      %mn 1
                      %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R \simeq \mathop{Rift}_L 1_D
              and this
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+lift"} Kan lift
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+lift"} absolute
          %p
            In this case, we get the counit as given by the universal cell
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                    %mi R
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mn 1
                      %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L R \to 1_D
          %p
            Dually, we have that for
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi D
                    %mo →
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R\colon D \to C
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi C
                  %mo →
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L \colon C \to D
            precisely if
          %ul
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Ran
                      %mi R
                    %msub
                      %mn 1
                      %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L \simeq \mathop{Ran}_R 1_D
              , and this Kan extension is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+extension"} absolute
          %p or, in terms of left Kan liftings:
          %ul
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Lift
                      %mi R
                    %msub
                      %mn 1
                      %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L \simeq \mathop{Lift}_R 1_C
              , and this Kan lifting is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+lift"} absolute
          %p
            This follows from the fact that the adjunction
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                  %mo ⊣
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L \dashv R
            %a{:href => "#PrePostcompositeAdjunctions"} induces
            adjunctions
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo ∘
                  %mi R
                  %mo ⊣
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo ∘
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} - \circ R \dashv - \circ L
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                    %mo ∘
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ⊣
                    %mi R
                    %mo ∘
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L \circ - \dashv R \circ -
          %p
            The formulations in terms of liftings generalize to (unenriched)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relative+adjoint"} relative adjoints
            by allowing an arbitrary functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi J
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
            in place of the identity; see there for more.
          %h3#TransformationOfAdjoints Transformation of adjoints
          %p
            There are several layers of generality at which one may consider a notion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphism"} homomorphism
            %em between
            adjoint functors.
          %p Here is a basic but important notion:
          %p
          #ConjugateTransformationOfAdjoints.num_defn
            %h6 Definition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conjugate+transformations+of+adjoints"}> conjugate transformations of adjoints
                )
              %br/
              Given a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pair"} pair
              of pairs of adjoint functors between the same
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categories"} categories
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi 𝒞
                            %munderover
                              %mrow
                                %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                                %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                                %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                                %mo ⊥
                                %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                                %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                                %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                              %munder
                                %mo ⟵
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi R
                                    %mn 1
                              %mover
                                %mo ⟶
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi L
                                    %mn 1
                            %mi 𝒟
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi 𝒞
                            %munderover
                              %mrow
                                %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                                %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                                %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                                %mo ⊥
                                %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                                %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                                %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                              %munder
                                %mo ⟵
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi R
                                    %mn 2
                              %mover
                                %mo ⟶
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi L
                                    %mn 2
                            %mi 𝒟
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\mathcal{C}
                    \\underoverset
                    {\underset{R_1}{\longleftarrow}}
                    {\overset{L_1}{\longrightarrow}}
                    {\;\;\; \bot \;\;\;}
                    \\mathcal{D}
                    \\\
                    \\mathcal{C}
                    \\underoverset
                    {\underset{R_2}{\longleftarrow}}
                    {\overset{L_2}{\longrightarrow}}
                    {\;\;\; \bot \;\;\;}
                    \\mathcal{D}
                    }
            %p
              then a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pair"} pair
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformations"} natural transformations
              between the adjoints of the same chirality, of this form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi λ
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mn 1
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mn 2
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi ρ
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi R
                      %mn 2
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi R
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\lambda \,\colon\, L_1 \to L_2
                    \\;\;\;\;\;\;
                    \\rho \,\colon\, R_2 \to R_1
            %p
              is called
              %em conjugate for
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "#MacLane71"}> MacLane (1971), §IV.7 (5)
              \&amp;rbrack; or a
              %em pseudo-transformation of
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "#HarpazPrasma15"}> Harpaz &amp; Prasma (2015), Sec. 2.2
              \&amp;rbrack; the given adjunctions if they make the following
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagram"} diagram
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformations"} natural transformations
              between
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-sets"} hom-sets
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commuting+diagram"} commute
