          %h2#References References
          %p
            For the basics, see any text on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+theory"} category theory
            (and see the references at
            = succeed ")," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunction"} adjunction
          %ul
            %li#MacLane71
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Saunders+MacLane"}> Saunders MacLane
                , Chapter IV of:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Categories+Work"} Categories for the working mathematician
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://link.springer.com/book/10.1007/978-1-4757-4721-8"} doi:10.1007/978-1-4757-4721-8
            %li#Borceux94
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Francis+Borceux"}> Francis Borceux
                , Section 3 in Volume 1 and Section 4.2 in Volume 2 of
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Handbook+of+Categorical+Algebra"} Handbook of Categorical Algebra
                (1994)
            %li#Johnstone
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+Johnstone"}> Peter Johnstone
                , first pages of
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sketches+of+an+Elephant"} Sketches of an Elephant
                (2022)
            %li
              %p
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry+of+physics+--+categories+and+toposes"} geometry of physics – categories and toposes
                  –
                  %a{:href => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/geometry+of+physics+--+categories+and+toposes#Adjunctions"} Adjunctions
          %p
            Though the definition of an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+equivalence"} adjoint equivalence
            appears in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck"} Grothendieck's
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tohoku"} Tohoku
            paper, the idea of adjoint functors in general goes back to
          %ul
            %li#Kan58
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Kan"}> Daniel Kan
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Adjoint functors
              %strong 87
              2 (1958) 294-329 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://www.jstor.org/stable/1993102"}> jstor:1993102
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            and in
            %a{:href => "monad#RelationToAdjunctionsAndMonadicity"} relation
            to
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/comonad"} co
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monads"} monads
            to
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+J.+Huber"}> Peter J. Huber
              , §4 in:
              = succeed "," do
                %em Homotopy theory in general categories
              %strong 144
              (1961) 361–385 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/BF01396534"}> doi:10.1007/BF01396534
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            and its fundamental relevance for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+theory"} category theory
            was highlighted in
          %ul
            %li#Freyd64
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+Freyd"}> Peter Freyd
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Abelian categories – An introduction to the theory of functors
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.maths.ed.ac.uk/~aar/papers/freydab.pdf"} pdf
            %li#Lawvere69
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/William+Lawvere"}> William Lawvere
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Adjointness in Foundations
                = succeed ")," do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.emis.de/journals/TAC/reprints/articles/16/tr16abs.html"} TAC
          %p
            The history of the idea that adjoint functors formalize aspects of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dialectics"} dialectics
            is recounted in
          %ul
            %li#Lambek82
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Joachim+Lambek"}> Joachim Lambek
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The Influence of Heraclitus on Modern Mathematics
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Scientific Philosophy Today: Essays in Honor of Mario Bunge
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/978-94-009-8462-2_6"} doi:10.1007/978-94-009-8462-2_6
              %p
                (more along these lines at
                = succeed ")" do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+modality"} adjoint modality
          %p See also:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Wikipedia,
                %a{:href => "http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Adjoint_functors"} Adjoint Functors
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/The+Catsters"} The Catsters
                (
                %a{:href => "http://www.youtube.com/view_play_list?p=54B49729E5102248"}> list
                )
          %p
            More on the notion of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transformation+of+adjoints"} transformation of adjoints
          %ul
            %li#HarpazPrasma15
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yonatan+Harpaz"}> Yonatan Harpaz
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Matan+Prasma"} Matan Prasma
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The Grothendieck construction for model categories
                %strong 281
                (2015) 1306-1363 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1404.1852"}> arXiv:1404.1852
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.aim.2015.03.031"} 10.1016/j.aim.2015.03.031
              %blockquote
                %p
                  (in the context of the
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+a+Grothendieck+construction"} model structure on a Grothendieck construction
